  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: db176a60e3b58b4408636b22a97519c4, type: 3}
  m_Name: WaterRecyclingEvent
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MarsEvent
  eventTitle: Water Recycling Problem
  eventDescription: Warning! The Mars outpost's water recycling system is operating
    below normal efficiency. Water reserves are becoming limited, and the crew depends
    on a reliable water supply for drinking, hygiene, and life support. You must
    decide how to restore water availability while managing the base's resources.
  targetSol: 5
  optionATitle: Repair Water Recycling System
  energyChangeA: -10
  lifeSupportChangeA: 20
  shieldChangeA: 0
  resultTitleA: Water Recycling Restored
  resultDescriptionA: The crew successfully repairs the water recycling system, restoring
    a reliable supply of clean water. Life support conditions improve significantly,
    but the repair consumes additional energy.
  optionBTitle: Implement Water Rationing
  energyChangeB: 5
  lifeSupportChangeB: -10
  shieldChangeB: 0
  resultTitleB: Water Rationing Implemented
  resultDescriptionB: The crew introduces strict water conservation measures to reduce
    resource consumption. Energy reserves improve because the recycling system operates
    at reduced capacity, but limited water availability places additional strain
    on life support.
  educationalExplanation: Water recycling is essential for long-duration space missions.
    NASA uses water recovery systems aboard the International Space Station to collect
    and purify water from sources such as humidity and wastewater. Recycling water
    reduces the amount of supplies that must be transported from Earth and helps
    support astronauts during extended missions.
  scientificSource: "NASA \u2014 Environmental Control and Life Support System"
  scientificSourceURL: https://www.nasa.gov/reference/environmental-control-and-life-support-system-eclss/
